# CLCA Protocol v3.4 — P4a_CONSTRUCTIONS
# Language: {{ lang.name }} ({{ lang.code }})

# PURPOSE
Produce a compact structural inventory of constructions that express
truth-domain meanings in this language. LIMIT EXAMPLES to ~2 per pattern.

Do NOT include:
- full paradigms
- extended morphological inventories
- idiomatic lists beyond 1–2 examples
- long commentary

# CONTEXT (from P1–P3):
{{ context }}

# EACH SECTION MUST INCLUDE:
- Pattern (structural description)
- 2 examples (native → transliteration → translation)
- 1–2 sentence structural note
- If construction absent: "NO COMMON EXPRESSION EXISTS"

# PATTERNS TO INVESTIGATE (if attested)
1. Attribution
2. Negative Attribution
3. Adnominal Modification
4. Become / Inchoative
5. Causative (or absence)
6. Abstract Nominalization
7. Agentive Nominalization (liar, truth-teller)
- Do NOT assume all patterns exist
- If no natural expression exists, write:
  (no common expression identified)
- If other construction types emerge naturally from the data, add them as additional numbered sections

# FORMAT (use exactly)
## 1. ATTRIBUTION
### Pattern
<pattern>
### Examples
- <example>
- <example>
### Notes
<brief structural note>

(Continue for sections 2–7, and any additional sections, in the same format)

# END
